sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Ceratites nodosus Schnakenberg Turing wavenumber at 26 µm (Ladinian, 240 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 85.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2, superseding the Pass-1 audit (overall 81.1). Activator diffusivity stays at the 26 µm solve. --gamma-factor 1.55 holds Du fixed and moves the selected wavelength from 25.6 µm to 29.3 µm. Resolved modes match the discrete Jacobian eigenvalue at Pearson r = 1.000 (RMSE ~ 1e-13). The continuous-symbol residual on that band is r = 0.976, RMSE 0.0037, which is the second-difference truncation and is reported rather than hidden. The full 30-mode continuous comparison remains r = 0.990. Equal diffusion and a 0.45-wavelength domain both decay. Specimen orientation cosine against the ocellus field is 0.995; row-wise wavelength CV is 0.675. Shell segmentation is unchanged (circularity 0.659). Chronoseries counts at 26 µm remain 703, 1250, and 1641. Still one photograph, and still no second assessor. Overall 85.8/100 (faithfulness 85.0, reproducibility 87.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 040c297c78d4c53dd775f1fcd23b9440ae0558db; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/ceratites_nodosus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 040c297c78d4c53dd775f1fcd23b9440ae0558db, image/png, 490995 B, 1848×1176 px, artifact_sha256 1b02be065e72e6facf0a0217d044283bee635e8911d3e6b287a4bafaeca27bae (sha256 1b02be065e72e6facf0a0217d044283bee635e8911d3e6b287a4bafaeca27bae), spec_fingerprint cef6ede1e830551276a963350aa3ce5c67a0cb0dabe081d68214d961e5f27b65. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: cef6ede1e830551276a963350aa3ce5c67a0cb0dabe081d68214d961e5f27b65; artifact_sha256: 1b02be065e72e6facf0a0217d044283bee635e8911d3e6b287a4bafaeca27bae; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ceratites_nodosus_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=ae965a155c4d31c3..., datasets/ceratites_nodosus_turing_wavelength_s0/ceratites_nodosus_specimen.jpg=3c37b42ed1bd3fde..., datasets/ceratites_nodosus_turing_wavelength_s0/ceratites_nodosus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=256f3874e2f667a0..., datasets/ceratites_nodosus_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=c4b089031d26801a..., datasets/ceratites_nodosus_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=54469d3595f1c16c...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-ceratites-nodosus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and diffusion-driven instability. | Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Meinhardt and Klingler (1987) interpret molluscan shell pigment as an activator-inhibitor pattern. | Boyajian and Lutz (1992) treat ammonoid suture complexity with a fractal descriptor. Campaign D_f values are 1.18, 1.34, and 1.55.; reconstructed_in_script: a = 0.062, b = 1.140, operating gamma = 1.15 times onset, Du solved for lambda = 2.56e-05 m and then held fixed. | Discrete-Jacobian eigenmode test on a 32-wavelength patch, plus the continuous-symbol residual. | Subcritical domain of 0.45 wavelengths, 12-bin orientation cosine, and row-wise wavelength CV.; transfer_boundary: Chroma on the growth GIF encodes the activator. Luminance of the last frame follows the photograph so the shell geometry remains the edge structure.; does_not_claim: That this photograph resolved a 26 µm pigment wavelength. | That Schnakenberg rates were measured in a Ceratites mantle. | That the continuous-symbol unstable-band correlation exceeds 0.98. It is 0.976. | That a second assessor scored this audit.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Still one shell photograph. It cannot confirm a 26 µm pigment; that limit stays open.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'Still no independent second assessor.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.858"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

